{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Usually, there are many different ways to divide polynomials. Here, we will use the method of polynomial long division.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n5x^2\\phantom{-17x+11}\n\\\\\nx-5|\\overline{5x^3-22x^2-17x+11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{5x^3-25x^2\\phantom{-17x+11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n3x^2-17x+11\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n5x^2+\\phantom{1}3x\\phantom{+11}\n\\\\\nx-5|\\overline{5x^3-22x^2-17x+11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{5x^3-25x^2\\phantom{-17x+11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n3x^2-17x+11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{3x^2-15x\\phantom{+11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n{}-2x+11\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":true,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{array}{r}\n5x^2+\\phantom{1}3x-\\phantom{1}2\n\\\\\nx-5|\\overline{5x^3-22x^2-17x+11}\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{5x^3-25x^2\\phantom{-17x+11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n3x^2-17x+11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{3x^2-15x\\phantom{+11}\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n{}-2x+11\n\\\\\n\\mathllap{-(}\\underline{{}-2x+10\\rlap )}\n\\\\\n1\n\\end{array}$","images":{},"replace":true,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We found that the quotient is $5x^2+3x-2$ and the remainder is $1$:\n\n$\\dfrac{5x^3-22x^2-17x+10}{x-5}=5x^2+3x-2+\\dfrac{1}{x-5}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Divide the polynomials.**  \n*The form of your answer should either be $p(x)$ or $p(x)+\\dfrac{k}{x-5}$ where $p(x)$ is a polynomial and $k$ is an integer.*\n\n$\\dfrac{5x^3-22x^2-17x+11}{x-5}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"buttonsVisible":"focused","considered":"correct","form":true,"functions":["f","g","h"],"key":0,"linterContext":{"contentType":"","h